*.sh text eol=lf
*.ps1 text eol=crlf
*.py text eol=lf
*.md text eol=lf
*.json text eol=lf
*.workflow.js text eol=lf

# ENG-95683 review — the JS toolchain is LF-ONLY, and this is a correctness rule, not a style one.
# `scripts/build-workflows.mjs` inlines `_workflow-core/*.mjs` into `*.workflow.js` (already pinned LF above) and
# then byte-compares the result. On a CRLF checkout the sources arrive CRLF, the generated file is pinned LF, and
# `--check` reports EVERY line as drifted — which makes the one gate protecting the generated artifacts unreadable
# rather than merely noisy, and hides real drift inside the noise (that is exactly how the blank-line drift this
# PR removes survived). `run-workflow-parity.mjs` fails the same way: it slices the shipped script and evaluates
# it, and CRLF breaks the slice with `SyntaxError: Unexpected token 'export'`.
# Every blob is ALREADY stored LF, so this changes only what lands in a working tree — no file content moves.
*.mjs text eol=lf
*.js text eol=lf
